      "text": "Lecture 1: Introduction and Peak Finding"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00001",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Lecture Overview"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00002",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Administrivia"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00003",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Course Overview"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00004",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• “Peak finding” problem — 1D and 2D versions"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00005",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Course Overview"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00006",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "This course covers:"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00007",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Efficient procedures for solving problems on large inputs (Ex: U.S. Highway Map, Human Genome)"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00008",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Scalability"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00009",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Classic data structures and elementary algorithms (CLRS text)"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00010",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Real implementations in Python"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00011",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Fun problem sets!"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00012",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "The course is divided into 8 modules — each of which has a motivating problem and problem set(s) (except for the last module). Tentative module topics and motivating problems are as described below:"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00013",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "1. Algorithmic Thinking: Peak Finding"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00014",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "2. Sorting & Trees: Event Simulation"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00015",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "3. Hashing: Genome Comparison"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00016",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "4. Numerics: RSA Encryption"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00017",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "5. Graphs: Rubik’s Cube"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00018",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "6. Shortest Paths: Caltech → MIT"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00019",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "7. Dynamic Programming: Image Compression"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00020",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 1,
      "section": null,
      "text": "8. Advanced Topics"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00021",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Peak Finder"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00022",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "One-dimensional Version"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00023",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Position 2 is a peak if and only if b ≥ a and b ≥ c. Position 9 is a peak if i ≥ h."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00024",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Figure 1: a-i are numbers"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00025",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Problem: Find a peak if it exists (Does it always exist?)"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00026",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Straightforward Algorithm"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00027",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Start from left"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00028",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "might be peak"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00029",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "θ(n) complexity worst case"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00030",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Figure 2: Look at n/2 elements on average, could look at n elements in the worst case"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00031",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 2,
      "section": null,
      "text": "What if we start in the middle? For the configuration below, we would look at n/2 elements. Would we have to ever look at more than n/2 elements if we start in the middle, and choose a direction based on which neighboring element is larger that the middle element?"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00032",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Can we do better?"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00033",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "look at n/2 position"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00034",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Figure 3: Divide & Conquer"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00035",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• If a[n/2] < a[n/2 − 1] then only look at left half 1 . . . n/2 −−− 1 to look for peak"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00036",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Else if a[n/2] < a[n/2 + 1] then only look at right half n/2 + 1 . . . n to look for peak"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00037",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Else n/2 position is a peak: WHY?"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00038",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "What is the complexity?"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00039",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "T (n) = T (n/2) + Θ(1) = Θ(1) + . . . + Θ(1) (log2(n) times) = Θ(log2(n)) '-v \" to compare a[n/2] to neighbors"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00040",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "In order to sum up the Θ(i)‘s as we do here, we need to find a constant that works for all. If n = 1000000, Θ(n) algo needs 13 sec in python. If algo is Θ(log n) we only need 0.001 sec. Argue that the algorithm is correct."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00041",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Two-dimensional Version"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00042",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "d n rows"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00043",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "m columns"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00044",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Figure 4: Greedy Ascent Algorithm: Θ(nm) complexity, Θ(n 2) algorithm if m = n"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00045",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 3,
      "section": null,
      "text": "a is a 2D-peak iff a ≥ b, a ≥ d, a ≥ c, a ≥ e"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00046",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Figure 5: Circled value is peak."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00047",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Attempt # 1: Extend 1D Divide and Conquer to 2D"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00048",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Pick middle column j = m/2."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00049",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Find a 1D-peak at i, j."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00050",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Use (i, j) as a start point on row i to find 1D-peak on row i."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00051",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Attempt #1 fails"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00052",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Problem: 2D-peak may not exist on row i"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00053",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 4,
      "section": null,
      "text": "End up with 14 which is not a 2D-peak."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00054",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Attempt # 2"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00055",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Pick middle column j = m/2"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00056",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Find global maximum on column j at (i, j)"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00057",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Compare (i, j − 1), (i, j), (i, j + 1)"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00058",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Pick left columns of (i, j − 1) > (i, j)"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00059",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Similarly for right"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00060",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• (i, j) is a 2D-peak if neither condition holds ← WHY?"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00061",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• Solve the new problem with half the number of columns."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00062",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "• When you have a single column, find global maximum and you‘re done."
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00063",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Example of Attempt #2"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00064",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "go with"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00065",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "find 21 21"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00066",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "pick this column 19 global max for this column"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00067",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "pick this column 17 global max for this column"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00068",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Complexity of Attempt #2"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00069",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "If T (n, m) denotes work required to solve problem with n rows and m columns"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00070",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "T (n, m) = T (n, m/2) + Θ(n) (to find global maximum on a column — (n rows))"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00071",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "T (n, m) = Θ(n) + . . . + Θ(n) ' -v \" log m = Θ(n log m) = Θ(n log n) if m = n"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc04facffd88-00072",
      "kind": "text",
      "start": null,
      "end": null,
      "page": 5,
      "section": null,
      "text": "Question: What if we replaced global maximum with 1D-peak in Attempt #2? Would that work?"
    }
  ]
}